ar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139332?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish","html_url":"https://github.com/hulkish","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-11-23T10:07:09Z","updated_at":"2018-11-23T10:15:26Z","body":"@sokra ok, so i added 3 tests for possible loader exceptions. While doing so, I stumbled on & fixed 2 more swallowed errors. See https://github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/8409/files#diff-d6308b00976bdf2edefc0f08dd6e1cafR842\r\n\r\nThe code path for this error would occur in both following cases:\r\n1. \"Module not found\" error (on loader `.js` file)\r\n2. Loader not returning buffer or string.\r\n\r\nBoth of these caused `this.processDependenciesQueue.add(module, callback)` to be invoked before the original error had a chance to be reported.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/comments/441199609/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/comments/441277583","html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/8409#issuecomment-441277583","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/8409","id":441277583,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTI3NzU4Mw==","user":{"login":"sokra","id":1365881,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU4ODE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1365881?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra","html_url":"https://github.com/sokra","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-11-23T16:10:59Z","updated_at":"2018-11-23T16:10:59Z","body":"> Seems like a tsdoc bug. NormalModule defines a `.error` prop.\r\n\r\nBut `Module` doesn't. Anyway it doesn't seem to be correct. If there is an error in the module `buildModule` should return it in the callback. Maybe the problem is deeper in NormalModule.build.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/comments/441277583/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/comments/441289919","html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/8409#issuecomment-441289919","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/8409","id":441289919,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTI4OTkxOQ==","user":{"login":"hulkish","id":139332,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTMzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139332?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish","html_url":"https://github.com/hulkish","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hulkish/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-11-23T17:18:04Z","updated_at":"2018-11-23T17:22:48Z","body":"> > Seems like a tsdoc bug. NormalModule defines a `.error` prop.\r\n> \r\n> But `Module` doesn't. Anyway it doesn't seem to be correct. If there is an error in the module `buildModule` should return it in the callback. Maybe the problem is deeper in NormalModule.build.\r\n\r\n@sokra Ok, so per my debugging via stepping through break point of this error... I guess my next thought would be to [change this line](https://github.com/webpack/webpack/blob/89e6bd23eea201a8b82f6fb67458986aa3b81a3e/lib/NormalModule.js#L521) to `return callback(err);`, right?\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/comments/441289919/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/comments/443874610","html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/8409#issuecomment-443874610","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/8409","id":443874610,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tb